## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/switch.html
- Summary (EN): Switch selects one of several input layers and passes it through as its output. The choice is controlled by a parameter, so the layer flowing downstream changes without rewiring the network.
- Résumé (FR) : Switch transmet l'une de ses entrées, choisie par un paramètre, sans qu'il soit nécessaire de recâbler le réseau en aval.

- Inputs meaning: ["input1: a series of possible input layers, indexed in order, and the Select Input parameter picks among them"]

- Key parameters: ["Select Input: chooses which input becomes the output, an out-of-range value uses the nearest valid input", "Output: chosen, the selected layer"]

- Caveats: ["The output takes the highest type among all inputs, and every input must be convertible to that type, so mixed input types can cause conversion issues", "Out-of-range values raise no error and silently fall back to the nearest input, which can hide an incorrect index", "Related nodes: Switch by Type, Switch If Wired, Two Way Switch If Wired"]

